 "about_text": "Timothy Hawkinson Gallery is a Los Angeles space on Beverly Boulevard that presents contemporary painting and drawing-based practices, largely through art-fair presentations such as NADA New York, NADA Miami, and Felix Art Fair. Its program pairs emerging and mid-career Los Angeles artists—among them Alise Spinella, Marc Pally, Mason Saltarrelli, and Samantha Yun Wall—with historically significant figures such as the Wiyot artist Rick Bartow and Mexico City-based Adrián S. Bará. The gallery emphasizes intuitive, process-driven abstraction, drawing, and works that explore the body, time, and cultural identity. It is a member of NADA and the Gallery Association Los Angeles (GALA).",
 "source_kind": "official",
